      {
        "type": "subhead",
        "content": "Argento's Visual Revolution"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Dario Argento's emergence in 1970 with \"The Bird with the Crystal Plumage\" marked a watershed moment for the genre, introducing a more modernist approach to giallo storytelling. Argento's technical innovations included elaborate tracking shots, extreme close-ups of murderous implements, and disorienting point-of-view sequences that would become his signature style. The film's success sparked a prolific period in giallo production, with Argento continuing to refine his approach through masterworks like \"Deep Red\" (1975) and \"Tenebrae\" (1982). His collaboration with cinematographer Luciano Tovoli brought an unprecedented level of visual sophistication to the genre, employing complex camera movements and architectural framing that transformed ordinary locations into labyrinthine spaces of dread and uncertainty."
      },
